{
  "title": "Food and drink",
  "note": "Du, de la, de l' mean \"some\" for things you don't count: du pain, de la viande, de l'eau. After a negative they become de: Je ne mange pas de viande. With verbs of liking (aimer, adorer, détester) use le, la, les: J'aime le fromage.",
  "src": { "t": "Français interactif, Chapitre 5 vocabulaire", "u": "https://laits.utexas.edu/fi/voc/05/" },
  "items": [
    { "c": "le pain", "a": "bread", "d": ["cheese", "cake"], "ex": "Je voudrais du pain, s'il vous plaît.", "exT": "I would like some bread, please." },
    { "c": "le fromage", "a": "cheese", "d": ["butter", "ham"] },
    { "c": "le beurre", "a": "butter", "d": ["milk", "cheese"] },
    { "c": "la viande", "a": "meat", "d": ["fish", "vegetables"] },
